Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 04:51:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(kanban): reuse exact publication membership derivation
 [daveey]

Why: sync-links still measured 0.544632% of a core after the alias cut,
above the unchanged <0.5% target. Captured source attribution identified
_Publications._index as the remaining largest ledger component. Each new
projection re-split and bucketed the same publication keys even though
only payloads changed. Board skip keys do not remove this upstream work.

Retain one bounded immutable derivation of the complete ordered SQL key
inventory. Re-read every key before reuse, and retain the original keyed
payload queries and projection-local membership lifetime. No clock TTL,
stream state, terminal decision, or owner liveness is memoized. Preserve
partial instance state on read failure without publishing that failure.

Rejected prefix discovery: a new key within an already-known profile
between has_other calls changed the predecessor's frozen membership.
Exact inventories retain that behavior and preserve SQL ordering/types.

Proof: original parent 0b0df50f31e5a795d7298517e5fc7d1b94a2795b has two
behavioral reuse failures / nine passes; candidate 24 regression cases
pass and all 11 exact-anchor mutants are killed. Whole scripts/check
passes against the actual parent; fresh-main gate follows publication.
20 counterbalanced captured source-composition pairs retain all 5842
ordered cards/slices; median thread CPU 224.1436765 -> 194.6616775 ms.
Diagnostic only: plain opener, frozen clock, absent local authority and
no cold durable carry. Live family acceptance is NOT yet established;
requires independent review/CI, normal deployment and new mature pair.
